ourse_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{l,m,n…,z}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d5abde8eb8680dcbb4dcc70fea7352b2885dc7a860860d6319e1046b38a3875" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{m,n,o…,z}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d5abde8eb8680dcbb4dcc70fea7352b2885dc7a860860d6319e1046b38a3875" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-105188" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{k,l,m,…,z}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d5abde8eb8680dcbb4dcc70fea7352b2885dc7a860860d6319e1046b38a3875" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $U = \\{ a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\}$ be the universal set and let $B = \\{ b, d, f \\}.$ What is $\\overline{B}?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/assets/25f40492b0466495519d6ff94859d0cef4c206e291d31eba2a980732b497af31.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/example-7163.json" "file_sha256" "f0f4c612ae4034cf6f2448643db2dea6733e95326e177702c97046f2d276c51d" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overline B,$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $B.$ To represent $\\overline B,$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $B,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/assets/daad235ef63e127e99bf3eec7b7bbe75fe6adb969f5b54ebb5a3fb010773b680.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $a,$ $c,$ $e,$ and $g.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $B.$ Therefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{B} = \\{ a,c,e,g \\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/example-7163.json" "file_sha256" "f0f4c612ae4034cf6f2448643db2dea6733e95326e177702c97046f2d276c51d" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $U = \\{ a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\}$ be the universal set and let $A = \\{ b, c, d, f, g \\}.$ What is $\\overline{A}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/example-7164.json" "file_sha256" "71e02415b594bec449f894dc35c3d17b341b8542d92b1f58628090cb3d47ff0a" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overline{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are $a$ and $e.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{A} = \\{ a, e \\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/example-7164.json" "file_sha256" "71e02415b594bec449f894dc35c3d17b341b8542d92b1f58628090cb3d47ff0a" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $U = \\{ 1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 30 \\}$ be the universal set and let $B = \\{ 5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 28 \\}.$ What is $\\overline{B}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/example-7165.json" "file_sha256" "f352a17f38a1f36cc6465b564ba909f15685dd4a9c5892120fd770d57e94bc8f" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overline{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integers $1$ through $30,$ while the set $B$ consists of the integers $5$ through $28.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $1,$ $2,$ $3,$ $4,$ $29,$ and $30.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{B} = \\{ 1,2,3,4,29,30 \\}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/example-7165.json" "file_sha256" "f352a17f38a1f36cc6465b564ba909f15685dd4a9c5892120fd770d57e94bc8f" "basis" 1256 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-86587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/02dabe7099c201f717885a05842e0cb8543bd01cccf0d6c52147f674cde15dce.png)\n\nLet $U={a,b,c,20,40}$ be the universal set and let $R={b,20,40}.$ What is the complement of $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/state.json" "file_sha256" "12749d077dc896c1b68da4c3a284382550d042f5617f4a8bfe2d56f01254efa3"} {"question" "q-86587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complement of $R,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{R},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $R.$ To represent $\\overset{―}{R},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $R,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/79900f22c35570b35cf10664768ecf4460a7953ddf7f91dac1893b3ce81339bf.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $a$ and $c.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $R.$ Therefore, the complement of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{R}={a,c}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/state.json" "file_sha256" "12749d077dc896c1b68da4c3a284382550d042f5617f4a8bfe2d56f01254efa3"} {"question" "q-86587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9e67c0752d98cbf07cc791a98fe64ee643774ef2741af6b019ff52a888f3dc2"} {"questi