{-20,-19,-18,…,20}$ is the universal set and $A={1,2,3,…,20},$ then $\\overset{―}{A}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/state.json" "file_sha256" "12749d077dc896c1b68da4c3a284382550d042f5617f4a8bfe2d56f01254efa3"} {"question" "q-1233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integers $-20$ through $20,$ while he set $A$ consists of the integers $1$ through $28.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the integers $-20$ through $0.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}={-20,-19,-18,…,0}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/state.json" "file_sha256" "12749d077dc896c1b68da4c3a284382550d042f5617f4a8bfe2d56f01254efa3"} {"question" "q-1233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f9e67c0752d98cbf07cc791a98fe64ee643774ef2741af6b019ff52a888f3dc2"} {"question" "q-1233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/state.json" "file_sha256" "12749d077dc896c1b68da4c3a284382550d042f5617f4a8bfe2d56f01254efa3"} {"question" "q-1233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{-20,-19,-18,…,0}"] ["math" "{-20,-19,-18,…,1}"] ["math" "{-20,-19,-18,…,20}"] ["math" "{1,2,3,…,20}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/